* ring51 -- 51-stage CMOS ring oscillator, MOS level=1
* Stage 1 is a NOR2 start-up gate: EN holds the ring in a known state until
* t=5ns, then releases it for deterministic oscillation in any simulator.
* Adapted from the tests/ ring-oscillator family; simple level-1 models only.
VDD vdd 0 DC 5
VEN en 0 PULSE(5 0 5n 0.5n 0.5n 1 2)
* stage 1: NOR2(en, s51) -> s1
MP1A p1a en vdd vdd PMOS1 L=1u W=8u
MP1B s1 s51 p1a vdd PMOS1 L=1u W=8u
MN1A s1 en 0 0 NMOS1 L=1u W=4u
MN1B s1 s51 0 0 NMOS1 L=1u W=4u
C1 s1 0 50f
* stage 2: inverter s1 -> s2
MP2 s2 s1 vdd vdd PMOS1 L=1u W=8u
MN2 s2 s1 0 0 NMOS1 L=1u W=4u
C2 s2 0 50f
* stage 3: inverter s2 -> s3
MP3 s3 s2 vdd vdd PMOS1 L=1u W=8u
MN3 s3 s2 0 0 NMOS1 L=1u W=4u
C3 s3 0 50f
* stage 4: inverter s3 -> s4
MP4 s4 s3 vdd vdd PMOS1 L=1u W=8u
MN4 s4 s3 0 0 NMOS1 L=1u W=4u
C4 s4 0 50f
* stage 5: inverter s4 -> s5
MP5 s5 s4 vdd vdd PMOS1 L=1u W=8u
MN5 s5 s4 0 0 NMOS1 L=1u W=4u
C5 s5 0 50f
* stage 6: inverter s5 -> s6
MP6 s6 s5 vdd vdd PMOS1 L=1u W=8u
MN6 s6 s5 0 0 NMOS1 L=1u W=4u
C6 s6 0 50f
* stage 7: inverter s6 -> s7
